From: Qualcommax NSS Builder
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: shrink RX rings for MX4200 v1

This builder only produces Linksys MX4200 v1 (512 MiB RAM) images.
The ppe-nss backports tree has no CPTCFG_ATH11K_MEM_PROFILE_512M
option, so a conditional on that symbol would leave both rings at 4096.

Shrink the remaining RX DMA buffer and monitor descriptor rings to
2048 entries. Do not touch the RXDMA refill *buffer length*, any other
ring, or the NSS Wi-Fi offload paths.

Based on https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/issues/24154
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp.h | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp.h
@@ -220,3 +220,3 @@
 #define DP_REO_STATUS_RING_SIZE		2048
-#define DP_RXDMA_BUF_RING_SIZE		4096
+#define DP_RXDMA_BUF_RING_SIZE		2048
 #define DP_RXDMA_REFILL_RING_SIZE	ATH11K_DP_RXDMA_REFILL_RING_SIZE
@@ -228,3 +228,3 @@
 #define DP_RXDMA_MONITOR_DST_RING_SIZE	ATH11K_DP_RXDMA_MONITOR_BUF_RING_SIZE
-#define DP_RXDMA_MONITOR_DESC_RING_SIZE	4096
+#define DP_RXDMA_MONITOR_DESC_RING_SIZE	2048
